  - key: Lunulo
    callsign: 6
    starter: 1
    given: "Lunulo"
    family: "Stormlight"
    speciesOne: 4
    speciesTwo: 5
    factionType: 8
    factionName: "Whisperkelp"
    homeworld: "Lanternfall"
    story: "Lunulo Stormlight grew up in the shadow of a dead Ark on Lanternfall.\n\nWhisperkelp trades in what other ports would rather keep. With Lunulo aboard, your crew will be sent to lift dispatches from rival ports, and the freshest news there will be yours to carry.\n\nThey keep a jar of every crystal they have ever missed."
  - key: Ovex
    callsign: 7
    starter: 1
    given: "Ovex"
    family: "Driftsong"
    speciesOne: 42
    speciesTwo: 40
    factionType: 11
    factionName: "The Glittering Heats"
    homeworld: "Cinder Bay"
    story: "Ovex Driftsong grew up mending nets on Cinder Bay.\n\nThe Glittering Heats put on exhibition runs in the brightest cells of the HyperSea. With Ovex aboard, your crew will be invited to fly them, skimming the course for every crystal on it.\n\nThey laugh at exactly the wrong moments."
  - key: Jodiola
    callsign: 8
    starter: 1
    given: "Jodiola"
    family: "Emberthorn"
    speciesOne: 29
    speciesTwo: 7
    factionType: 14
    factionName: "Harbour Watch"
    homeworld: "Mirrorfen"
    story: "Jodiola Emberthorn spent a childhood racing skiffs on Mirrorfen.\n\nThe Harbour Watch answers every distress call in the HyperSea. With Jodiola aboard, your crew will be sent to derelicts with crews stranded aboard, and stay until everyone is safe.\n\nThey name every vessel they fly, and apologise to it after a hard landing."
  - key: Pekoar
    callsign: 9
    starter: 1
    given: "Pekoar"
    family: "Starwright"
    speciesOne: 21
    speciesTwo: 44
    factionType: 6
    factionName: "The Unmapped"
    homeworld: "the Silver Lane"
    story: "Pekoar Starwright spent a childhood racing skiffs on the Silver Lane.\n\nThe The Unmapped sends crews where no one has been. With Pekoar aboard, your crew will be asked to survey uncharted places, and to follow chart fragments wherever they lead.\n\nThey cannot resist a dare."
  - key: Quibemo
    callsign: 10
    starter: 1
    given: "Quibemo"
    family: "Ashstone"
    speciesOne: 44
    speciesTwo: 30
    factionType: 11
    factionName: "The Glittering Heats"
    homeworld: "Stillwater"
    story: "Quibemo Ashstone grew up sorting crystals in a market stall on Stillwater.\n\nThe Glittering Heats puts on exhibition runs wherever there is a crowd. With Quibemo aboard, your crew will be invited to fly them, skimming the course for every crystal along it.\n\nThey cannot resist a dare."
  - key: Mamaola
    callsign: 11
    starter: 1
    given: "Mamaola"
    family: "Crestmark"
    speciesOne: 35
    speciesTwo: 25
    factionType: 9
    factionName: "The Patient Harvest"
    homeworld: "the Glass Shoals"
    story: "Mamaola Crestmark grew up in the shadow of a dead Ark on the Glass Shoals.\n\nThe Patient Harvest knows when the blooms of the HyperSea will open. With Mamaola aboard, your crew will be sent to harvest them while they last.\n\nThey name every vessel they fly, and apologise to it after a hard landing."
  - key: Tanuwen
    callsign: 12
    starter: 1
    given: "Tanuwen"
    family: "Spindlespark"
    speciesOne: 2
    speciesTwo: 47
    factionType: 14
    factionName: "Harbour Watch"
    homeworld: "Ember Deep"
    story: "Tanuwen Spindlespark learned to fly before they could read on Ember Deep.\n\nHarbour Watch answers the distress calls nobody else will. With Tanuwen aboard, your crew will be sent to derelicts where crews are stranded, to hold on until everyone is aboard.\n\nThey keep score of everything, including naps."
  - key: Wyve
    callsign: 13
    starter: 1
    given: "Wyve"
    family: "Stillline"
    speciesOne: 33
    speciesTwo: 28
    factionType: 1
    factionName: "Amber Ledger Guild"
    homeworld: "Rimehollow"
    story: "Wyve Stillline was raised among reef gardeners on Rimehollow.\n\nThe Amber Ledger Guild insures cargo across the HyperSea, so it needs crews to carry its dispatches and see its convoys safe to ports where trouble is brewing. With Wyve aboard, that work comes to you.\n\nThey cannot resist a dare."
  - key: Delliar
    callsign: 14
    starter: 1
    given: "Delliar"
    family: "Brinewater"
    speciesOne: 20
    speciesTwo: 2
    factionType: 3
    factionName: "House Albrine"
    homeworld: "Brackenmouth"
    story: "Delliar Brinewater spent a childhood racing skiffs on Brackenmouth.\n\nHouse Albrine holds cores in the green reaches of the HyperSea. Fly with Delliar and the house will ask your crew to patrol them, to answer its calls for aid, and to retake the ones another domain has taken.\n\nThey hum off-key during every jump."
  - key: Delsoko
    callsign: 15
    starter: 1
    given: "Delsoko"
    family: "Tidehook"
    speciesOne: 39
    speciesTwo: 24
    factionType: 8
    factionName: "Whisperkelp"
    homeworld: "the Kelp Throne"
    story: "Delsoko Tidehook was apprenticed to a cartographer on the Kelp Throne.\n\nWhisperkelp hears every secret that moves between ports. With Delsoko aboard, your crew will be sent to lift dispatches from rival ports, and carry the freshest news home first.\n\nThey keep score of everything, including naps."
  - key: Nemaix
    callsign: 16
    starter: 1
    given: "Nemaix"
    family: "Hollowline"
    speciesOne: 27
    speciesTwo: 16
    factionType: 15
    factionName: "The Ninefold Shell"
    homeworld: "Shellmouth"
    story: "Nemaix Hollowline was apprenticed to a cartographer on Shellmouth.\n\nThe Ninefold Shell keeps shrines across the HyperSea and the rite of nine that links them. With Nemaix aboard, your crew will be asked to hold a shrine through its vigil, and in time to join the ninefold rite.\n\nThey talk to the Ark at night and insist it answers."
  - key: Brilolia
    callsign: 17
